  "bodyText": "What to Expect on Sunday\n\nWelcome and Check-In\n\nAt each entrance, all ages are invited to check-in with a greeter.\n\nThe Greeters can direct you where you need to go,\nand answer questions you may have.\n\nChildren will receive a name tag for nursery or children's church.\n\nTo see what is happening in the Church this week, click below\n\nSunday School\n\n9:30 - 10:15\n\nIntergenerational Bible Study (B-04)\n\nLed by Jim Butler, this intergenerational Bible Study includes adults of all ages.\n\nFriendship Class (B-05)\n\nLed by Pastor Jonathan, this class primarily consists of a mix of couples with children at home, but is open to adults of all ages.\n\nYouth Large Group\n\n(201)\n\nSixth through twelfth (6th-12th) grade students join in discussions about life and faith.\n\nChildren's Sunday School (B-03 & 104)\n\n6 weeks - 3 years: Nursery\n\n(104)\n\nChildren's Worship Arts Play and practice in music, choir, scripture reading, and more (B-03).\n\nFellowship\n\n10:15 - 10:40\n\nDonut [Semi-] Hour\n(Fellowship Hall)\n\nBetween Bible study and Worship, join in a time of fellowship (and, of course, donuts)!\n\nWorship\n\n10:45 (Sanctuary)\n\nNursery Care (104)\n\nFor children ages 3 and younger, nursery care is available throughout the service.\n\nFamily Room (105)\n\nFor little ones and parents who need to step out during service, this room provides toys, a live stream, rocking chairs, nursing privacy, and a changing table for all who desire it.\n\nChildren's Church (B-03 & 102)\n\nStudents preschool - fifth grade will be dismissed to Children's Church during the service.\n\nThere are two classes.\n\nPreschool - 2nd grade: Kickstart Children's Church (102)\n\n3rd - 5th grade: The Underground Children's Church (B-03)\n\nCommunion\n\nA service with the whole church family.\n\nThe first Sunday of each month is communion Sunday.\n\nTo allow the whole church family to participate, there is no Children's Church (nursery care and our \"family room\" are always available).\n\nWe will all worship together in a service intentionally planned for all ages.\n\nSanctuary\n\nWelcome Center\n\nChurch Office\n\nFrequently asked questions\n\nHow do I find the church?\n\nThe church is located in downtown Muncie at 309 East Adams Street. Google maps will take you to the correct place. Our parking lot is located on the Adams Street side. The most common doors people use are the Adams Street entrance at our circular drive (wheelchair accessible), the large wooden front doors which go into the sanctuary, or the Jefferson Street side doors which enter our main hallway near the church offices.\n\nWhat should I wear?\n\nAre there nursery care or children’s worship during service?\n\nIs your building accessible / ADA compliant?\n\nAm I allowed to take the Lord’s Supper (communion?)\n\nI don’t have a background in the Christian religion / I’m not sure what I believe. Will that be a problem if I want to visit?\n\nWhat if I have other questions?\n\nLearn About Our Ministry\n\nThere are many areas of ongoing ministry at First Baptist Muncie, look below for more information on each!\n\nThe Worship Ministry at FBCM understands that Christian worship is a lifestyle centered around responding to the revealed God of the Bible.\n\nChildren\n\nChildren learn about the great big story of God's love each Sunday and throughout the year through age-appropriate lessons, games, and activities.\n\nYouth\n\nYouth encourage one another in their faith and grow in spiritual maturity together while having a lot of fun.\n\nAdult\n\nAdult Ministry aims to engage adults of all ages in intentional discipleship so we may follow Jesus and become more like him - full of grace and truth.\n\nOutreach\n\nWith our ministry partners, we share the mercy and love that God has shown us with others.\n\nWe want to share the love of Christ with Muncie and the world!\n\n[Button] See what’s happening this Sunday -> https://fbcmuncie.churchcenter.com/home\n\n[Button] Learn More -> https://www.fbcmuncie.org/worship\n\n[Button] Learn More -> https://www.fbcmuncie.org/children\n\n[Button] Learn More -> https://www.fbcmuncie.org/youth\n\n[Button] Learn More -> https://www.fbcmuncie.org/adult\n\n[Button] Learn More -> https://www.fbcmuncie.org/outreach",
